<h2>From Section 41A CrPC to Section 35 BNSS</h2>
<p>The Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, in force since 1 July 2024, folds the old Sections 41 and 41A CrPC into a single Section 35. The structure is familiar: sub-section (1) states when arrest without warrant is permissible, and for offences punishable up to seven years it demands recorded reasons tied to necessity; sub-section (3) requires a notice of appearance where arrest is not justified; sub-sections (4) to (6) deal with the duty to comply and the consequences of default; and sub-section (7) adds fresh protection for the infirm and for persons above sixty.</p>
<div class="compare">
